From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Opsero <noreply@opsero.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 17:06:30 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] drm: xlnx: mixer: accept MEDIA_BUS_FMT_FIXED from the bridge
 chain

With xlnx_mixer.connect_drm_bridge=1 and a bridge chain that carries no
bus format information (for example a panel-dpi panel bridge: its
connector reports no bus format, so the chain offers only
MEDIA_BUS_FMT_FIXED), xlnx_mix_crtc_select_output_bus_format() finds no
match for the mixer's output format and returns 0. The bridge chain
atomic check then fails with -ENOTSUPP (-524) and no mode can be set:

  Bridge atomic check failed: -524

A FIXED input format means the format is fixed by the hardware behind
the bridge, so return the mixer's own output bus format in that case.

Signed-off-by: Opsero <noreply@opsero.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/xlnx/xlnx_mixer.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/xlnx/xlnx_mixer.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/xlnx/xlnx_mixer.c
index 1e0a129..61ff653 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/xlnx/xlnx_mixer.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/xlnx/xlnx_mixer.c
@@ -3093,6 +3093,16 @@ xlnx_mix_crtc_select_output_bus_format(struct drm_crtc *crtc,
 		if (in_bus_fmts[i] == mixer->mixer_hw.out_bus_format)
 			return mixer->mixer_hw.out_bus_format;
 
+	/*
+	 * A bridge chain without bus format information (e.g. a panel-dpi
+	 * panel bridge, whose connector reports no bus format) only offers
+	 * MEDIA_BUS_FMT_FIXED: the format is fixed by the hardware, so keep
+	 * the mixer's own output format instead of failing the atomic check.
+	 */
+	for (i = 0; i < num_in_bus_fmts; ++i)
+		if (in_bus_fmts[i] == MEDIA_BUS_FMT_FIXED)
+			return mixer->mixer_hw.out_bus_format;
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
